  note    = {FULL TEXT READ 2026-09-04 (PDF supplied by user). Fourth Gallardo \& Aldridge paper found in this review. BIOMOD ensemble SDMs (the exact tool named in this project's proposal, Section 8) for TWO species already in this project's shortlist -- zebra mussel (Dreissena polymorpha) and signal crayfish (Pacifastacus leniusculus) -- each paired against one endangered native species (depressed river mussel Pseudanodonta complanata; white-clawed crayfish Austropotamobius pallipes) to compute range overlap under current and 2050 climate, Europe scale. Two SEPARATE invasive-native pairs analyzed in parallel, not a combined multi-invader stack -- not a threat to the compounding-risk metric specifically, but directly relevant precedent for the Q4 biodiversity-stakes overlay and a precursor to Lee et al. (2025)'s RHM approach. Confirms Gallardo \& Aldridge's own internal citation numbering (seen in Gallardo2018's reference list as "Gallardo and Aldridge, 2013c") -- there are at least three 2013 Gallardo \& Aldridge papers (dirty dozen = a, priority-setting/Ecological Applications = b, this one = c).}
